WEBVTT

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.690
Let's change IDOLiSH7's center.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:08.020
Don't use your poor health as an 
excuse for your irresponsibility.

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.030
I keep causing trouble for everyone.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:12.990
I keep holding the group back.

00:00:13.750 --> 00:00:17.450
I accept your proposal to change centers.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.520
Discover...

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.500
Let's go find it together (the future)

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.740
There's a glimmer I want 
to realize with you

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:32.810
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:38.150
Wow...

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:48.690
As though we're weaving together 
our aspiration (Sing a song)

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:53.780
The melody paints a giant constellation

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.530
No matter what tomorrow's like,
 it won't betray us

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:04.250
We'll change even the harshest environments

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.930
(Some day!) A magnificent Dream

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:09.470
(Always!) The evening calm's Mild

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:14.880
Aim for distant lands! "Be with you!"

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.430
Discover...

00:01:16.430 --> 00:01:20.220
A map of the stars (if we follow it)

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:25.850
We'll never look down Smile for you!

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.240
Night sky

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:31.110
Let's run across it together (to the future)

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.580
There's a glimmer I want 
to realize with you

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:39.160
Look, it's right here waiting 
for us (Let's jump!)

00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.450
Wow...

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.010
#04 A New Form

00:01:56.330 --> 00:02:00.250
If we keep things as they are, Nanase-san 
will only continue to lose confidence.

00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:04.010
Our namesake show would begin airing, 
we'd be receiving a lot of attention,

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:06.730
and Nanase-san would be 
standing at our center...

00:02:06.730 --> 00:02:10.150
Everyone would remember the names 
of both IDOLiSH7 and Nanase-san.

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.400
That was my dream.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.030
Iori-san.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:17.480
There's no point in lamenting it.

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:19.840
Let's change our focus and move forward.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:23.670
I understand your and 
Riku-san's frustration.

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:26.680
Thank you for helping me realize this.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:31.770
Without you, I would have destroyed 
Nanase-san before turning him into a star.

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.880
I'm glad you're our manager.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:40.440
The production of our concert
 the other day was fantastic, as well.

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:41.800
You've got talent.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.600
I'm flattered to hear you say that.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.610
I'm fawning over you.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:47.910
Can't you see that?

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:52.420
Iori-san, you're an awkward person.

00:02:52.420 --> 00:02:53.930
Are you making fun of me?

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:56.980
No. I think you're very charming.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:02.510
Whether things are going well or poorly,
 you captivate people's hearts.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:06.420
Because this is such an important time,

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:10.210
I'm trusting you to be 
the center of IDOLiSH7.

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.920
Iori will be the center instead of me?

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:18.670
Considering what's happened until now, 
I believe it's our best strategy.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:21.290
To protect our seven man team.

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:23.510
To protect IDOLiSH7.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:27.040
We've changed centers before 
depending on the song.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:28.530
It's the same thing.

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:31.690
Just think of me as our pinch-hitter 
until you've fully recovered.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:36.070
Sorry for causing all this trouble.

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.330
It's simple division of labor.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:40.980
We should be covering for 
each other's weaknesses.

00:03:42.860 --> 00:03:43.910
Thanks.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.530
Honestly, I'm relieved.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:49.230
I was anxious every morning 
before going to work.

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:52.220
Seriously, thank you.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:57.290
If you're okay with all this, I've got
 nothing to say on the subject.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:01.010
Yeah. No matter what we look 
like, we'll keep supporting you.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:01.970
You're right.

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:02.930
Yes.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:03.510
Yeah.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.660
Thanks, guys.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.150
I'd better find some 
way to thank you, Iori.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:10.060
Less than a thousand yen's 
worth of snacks again?

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:12.150
I'll spend more this time.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.440
I'll buy you whatever you want.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:17.250
I look forward to it.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.520
Changing centers, huh?

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:24.340
Riku seemed to be struggling.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:26.530
This is probably for the best.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:32.830
No matter what our group looks like, 
our name and our bond will never change.

00:04:32.830 --> 00:04:34.540
By the way, Mitsuki...

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:38.630
<b>TV Anime Series</b>

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:38.630
I'd like to watch <i>Cocona</i> sometime soon.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:42.340
No way. I still have other 
shows I need to watch first.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.010
Oh. You're studying so hard.

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.440
We have to make this a success.

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:51.130
I want to liven up the show and 
have people learn more about us.

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:53.810
Besides, I'm having a ton 
of fun right now!

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:57.900
Earning someone's recognition 
makes me happy.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:00.500
I'm happy, too.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:02.770
I'm a fan of yours, Mitsuki.

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:05.570
It makes me happy when 
you receive praise.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:08.170
You're kind and strong.

00:05:08.170 --> 00:05:11.140
You should have received praise sooner.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:14.070
Congratulations, Mitsuki.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:15.830
Nagi.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.820
Can we watch <i>Cocona </i>now—

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:18.260
No.

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:19.170
Oh...

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.790
Yotsuba-san, the bath is free.

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:26.180
Iorin.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:27.540
Yes?

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.470
This is tough.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:33.470
Please don't. He probably hasn't noticed.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.480
I see.

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:38.330
Does MEZZO" never experience 
anything like this?

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:41.410
We're too different.

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:44.150
It's too difficult to compare us.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:56.870
Please prepare for the show.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:05:58.990
Got it.

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:01.000
Ichi, are you nervous?

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:04.000
This is our first live show 
since you became the center.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:05.820
Please don't compare me to him.

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:07.850
Hey! What does that mean?

00:06:07.850 --> 00:06:10.300
Exactly what it sounds like.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.070
You're so annoying.

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:16.170
But you're helping me out, either way.

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:17.940
Don't be nervous. Good luck!

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:20.190
I told you, I'm not nervous.

00:06:20.620 --> 00:06:23.440
It's time for our next guest!

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.470
<i>Please.</i>

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:33.990
<i>Please let the new form of IDOLiSH7...</i>

00:06:33.990 --> 00:06:36.010
Huh? What?

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:37.500
No way!

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:39.000
<i>...be accepted by everyone.</i>

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:41.680
IDOLiSH7 has turned over a new 
leaf, changing their center

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:44.410
from Nanase Riku-kun to Izumi Iori-kun!

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:47.260
They'll be singing "Perfection Gimmick"!

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:58.770
Are you bored? Knock Knock on your door

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:02.480
Open your eyes and Ready not? Ready go

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:06.190
The dress code is your Heart dance

00:07:06.190 --> 00:07:09.450
Let's get tonight's show started

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:13.160
Be free Colorful beat

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:16.870
Woah oh that is the Only one chord

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:20.620
Chest-piercing Scene It's kaleidoscope!

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:25.250
Tonight ignite, our hearts will spark!

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:32.720
I'll set a Perfection Gimmick on 
you, I want you to feel Amazing

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:40.140
I want to show you Another face 
more grown up than my usual self

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:47.700
Perfection Gimmick, we are 
Jugglers sparkling in the night

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:49.340
I'll seduce you

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:55.800
With a yet unknown and special 
spell I'll be Drawing the delight

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:58.780
Trust me

00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:03.190
<i>It's so easy to dance.</i>

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:06.600
<i>He may be my younger brother, 
but he's so stable.</i>

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:09.500
<i>Ichi sees the whole picture so clearly.</i>

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:14.030
<i>He's not an exceptionally 
good singer like Rikkun,</i>

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:15.010
<i>but he's easy to perform around.</i>

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:17.900
<i>He's so smart.</i>

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:20.060
<i>The audience is beginning 
to accept us, too.</i>

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:25.270
<i>He's amazing. I thought 
he'd be more nervous.</i>

00:08:25.670 --> 00:08:27.790
<i>I'd better work harder.</i>

00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:36.180
I'll set a Perfection Gimmick on you, 
I want you to feel Amazing

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:43.410
I want to show you Another face 
more grown up than my usual self

00:08:43.410 --> 00:08:51.220
Perfection Gimmick, we are 
Jugglers sparkling in the night

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:49.220
I was worried what would happen since 
they suddenly changed their center.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:50.380
Their balance is good.

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:55.630
...a yet unknown and special 
spell I'll be Drawing the delight

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:58.700
It's wonder night

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:10.070
We're IDOLiSH7. Thank you.

00:09:13.070 --> 00:09:15.200
Did you see IDOLiSH7 yesterday?

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:17.900
They suddenly made the 
younger Izumi their center!

00:09:17.900 --> 00:09:19.070
I was so surprised!

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:20.900
Their center's 17 years old.

00:09:20.900 --> 00:09:21.610
Really?

00:09:21.610 --> 00:09:24.140
The little guy who talks a lot is funny.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:26.380
Their show started the other
 night and it's good, too!

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:29.570
What's it called? You know, uh... <i>Lovely</i>...

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:32.670
<i>Lovely Night With You!</i>

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:32.670
<b>Lovely Night With You!</b>

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:34.300
Thank you, I7!

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:34.300
I'm cheering for you!

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:37.430
<i>Lovely Night With You</i> is starting.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.890
Thanks for watching 
again today, everyone.

00:09:38.300 --> 00:09:41.680
<b>Lovely Night With You!</b>

00:09:39.890 --> 00:09:41.680
Thank you!

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:47.610
This is our third episode. 
Do you remember our names yet?

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.730
Uh-huh, uh-huh. You're not totally sure yet.

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:53.940
Okay, then. Let's introduce 
our members again.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:56.700
Thank you, I7!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:56.700
I'm cheering for you!

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:56.700
Ready, cameraman? Here we go.

00:09:57.020 --> 00:09:59.660
Iori, Riku, Yamato-san, 
Nagi, Sogo, Tamaki!

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:01.790
What a sloppy introduction.

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:04.080
One more time, then.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:07.210
Iori, Riku, Yamato-san, 
Nagi, Sogo, Tamaki!

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:10.490
And I'm Izumi Mitsuki!

00:10:10.490 --> 00:10:11.920
You only gave your own full name!

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.840
Thank you, I7!

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:13.840
I'm cheering for you!

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.110
That kid's good at MCing.

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:20.760
I haven't seen an idol who's this good 
on variety shows since Re:vale's Momo.

00:10:22.570 --> 00:10:25.220
Everyone's loving <i>Lovely Night With You</i>.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:29.200
Yes. Mitsuki-san in particular has 
received invitations to appear

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:30.730
on other variety programs.

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:33.420
Iori-san has been received 
favorably as our center,

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:35.480
and everyone's personalities 
are starting to show.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:38.290
Fan club memberships are up, too.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:41.170
And the Zero Arena inaugural 
show is waiting for us as well.

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:43.430
I'm actually thinking 
about riding this wave

00:10:43.430 --> 00:10:46.450
and releasing a new song for MEZZO".

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:48.380
I think that's a good idea.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:52.130
Their fans have been requesting 
a new single for a while now.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:56.080
I believe MEZZO" has received an 
offer to playing the leading roles

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:58.670
in a drama with their new 
song as the main theme.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:02.140
That offer is going to be rescinded, though...

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:06.890
What? I heard they were working on the 
script with the two of them in mind.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:09.230
Is it sponsor problems?

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:13.020
It's not Sogo-san. It's Tamaki-san.

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:17.530
Oh, right. I heard the director 
is very strict with manners.

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:21.660
Yes. He claimed that Tamaki-san went 
on a rampage during that special last year

00:11:21.660 --> 00:11:24.100
and hospitalized some of the staff.

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:26.130
Hospitalized?!

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:29.420
Rumors easily become 
exaggerated in our industry.

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:34.000
I asked to meet with him and 
clear up any misunderstandings,

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:37.030
but he said he'd only be 
willing to work with Sogo-san.

00:11:37.030 --> 00:11:38.760
What do you want to do?

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:40.710
If Sogo-san stars in the drama,

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:44.760
it's possible that they'll use 
MEZZO"'s new song as the main theme.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:48.770
But at this rate, we'll lose the opportunity
 to dispel the misunderstandings

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:50.270
around Tamaki-san forever.

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:53.250
I'm planning to insist 
on it being both of them.

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:56.770
Got it. I'll work on my 
minced chicken recipe.

00:11:57.580 --> 00:11:58.900
Minced chicken?

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:01.580
It's the director's favorite food.

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:04.550
He might appreciate some as a gift.

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:06.820
Banri-kun's recipe is good.

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:08.410
Thank you.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:10.470
We'll have to work on improving

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:13.030
Tamaki-kun's mental awareness
 in order to resolve this.

00:12:13.030 --> 00:12:16.290
Naturally, as his closest associate,

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:18.200
it'll become necessary 
for Sogo-kun as well.

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:21.050
Improve his awareness?

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:24.160
Their voices make a great pair.

00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:27.310
They draw out and highlight 
each other's appeal.

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:30.390
They should be able to achieve 
that kind of relationship.

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:34.730
The title is "Pieces of Love."

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:37.060
This song will help MEZZO" be reborn.

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:40.530
It's an opportunity for 
the two of them to grow.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:44.570
<b>Elevators</b>

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.570
Tamaki-kun, I won't tell 
you not to improvise.

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:47.460
But if you change too much, then 
there's no point in us dancing—

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:49.720
<i>God</i>, shut up already!

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:51.970
There's something called 
"feeling," you know!

00:12:51.970 --> 00:12:54.960
Are you just a robot who 
dances as he's told?!

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:56.960
You're changing too much on your own!

00:12:56.960 --> 00:12:59.000
Show some respect for the choreographer!

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:00.810
It's <i>always</i> about other people with you!

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:04.880
But you're always telling <i>me</i> no, and you
 never say the real important stuff!

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:06.050
What?

00:13:06.710 --> 00:13:11.560
You know how you sometimes 
apologize to people by yourself?

00:13:11.560 --> 00:13:13.550
Is that my fault?

00:13:14.110 --> 00:13:15.150
No.

00:13:15.150 --> 00:13:16.860
What is it, then?!

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:19.310
If something's up, you should tell me!

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:23.070
I tell you when it's something
 I want you to fix, like right now.

00:13:24.690 --> 00:13:30.370
The manager said our new song is 
an opportunity for us to be reborn.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:34.500
You're right. We can't keep 
going like this forever.

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:36.890
What?

00:13:36.890 --> 00:13:37.960
Be a wall for second.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:39.180
A wall?

00:13:39.180 --> 00:13:41.460
Should I spread my arms? Should I jump?

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:43.090
Don't do anything to attract attention!

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:47.370
Thank you very much for coming today.

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:49.020
I have high hopes for this show.

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:51.690
It's a music program with 
TRIGGER as the main MC.

00:13:51.690 --> 00:13:55.270
I don't expect to lose to our 
competitor, <i>Lovely Night With You</i>.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:14:00.270
I'd like to thank FSC again for 
agreeing to be our sponsor.

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:03.530
FSC? Isn't that your dad's company?

00:14:06.410 --> 00:14:08.570
Let's not worry about other 
shows airing in our time slot.

00:14:08.570 --> 00:14:11.610
They start airing a month after us.

00:14:11.610 --> 00:14:14.490
In the meantime, let's gather 
all the viewers we can.

00:14:14.490 --> 00:14:15.950
She's right, Sogo-san.

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:17.180
But...

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:19.780
We're prepared for that much, at least.

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:21.460
Yamato-san.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.490
Besides, we have other strengths.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:25.270
Strengths?

00:14:25.270 --> 00:14:27.630
Yamato-san was offered a major job!

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:30.970
That's great, Yama-san! 
You got a major job.

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:36.490
I prefer the laid-back approach 
of doing lots of little jobs.

00:14:36.490 --> 00:14:37.900
What kind of job is it?

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:42.020
The popular police drama <i>Mission</i> 
starring Re:vale's Yuki-san

00:14:42.020 --> 00:14:44.050
is getting a movie.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:47.540
Yamato-san received an offer 
for an important role.

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:49.390
Fantastic!

00:14:48.190 --> 00:14:50.410
That's a huge step up for you!

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:51.250
I'm not doing it.

00:14:51.250 --> 00:14:51.690
What?

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:54.430
Turn them down. I'm not 
moving to the silver screen.

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:57.190
Yuki-san will be there, though.

00:14:57.190 --> 00:14:59.790
I'm not doing it. End of story.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.950
This is a rare opportunity!

00:15:01.950 --> 00:15:03.740
Everyone else is working so hard.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:08.340
Yamato, I avoid being nosy on principle.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:10.970
Good principle to have. 
Keep it up until the day you die.

00:15:10.970 --> 00:15:13.090
Please remove your glasses.

00:15:13.090 --> 00:15:14.980
Don't immediately go back on your word.

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:16.850
Why do you hide it?

00:15:16.850 --> 00:15:20.060
I know your secret, Yamato.

00:15:20.060 --> 00:15:22.710
Stop hiding the truth and tell us.

00:15:22.710 --> 00:15:25.590
We're co-members. We're best friends.

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:30.530
Really? I know something, too, 
Rokuya Nagi. Your true identity.

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:39.080
Oh. On the night of a full moon, did you 
see the tail on the long shadow I cast?

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.870
It's more scandalous than that.

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:44.010
Shall we go watch 
<i>Cocona-chan</i> in your room?

00:15:44.010 --> 00:15:47.250
Yes, yes! I'm all for it!

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:52.630
Wh-What did he say?

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:54.750
Looks like he guessed right.

00:15:54.750 --> 00:15:56.760
He said yes a bunch of times.

00:15:57.860 --> 00:15:59.420
Yamato.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:02.860
I allowed you to dodge the subject.

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:04.850
You should be grateful.

00:16:04.850 --> 00:16:07.780
You're a difficult person.

00:16:07.780 --> 00:16:09.860
It pains me that you even 
turn against your friends

00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:13.130
when the subject of 
your secret comes up.

00:16:15.070 --> 00:16:17.210
What are you afraid of?

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:20.370
I wish you'd have more faith in us.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:27.580
I pray you'll someday find the courage
 to reveal your secret to us.

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:30.880
<b>IDOLiSH7 Greenroom</b>

00:16:29.370 --> 00:16:32.760
Congratulations on the start
 of your broadcast!

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:34.760
Momo-san, Yuki-san.

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:37.140
We saw <i>Lovely Night With You</i>.

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:38.900
It was so much fun!

00:16:38.900 --> 00:16:42.020
So, when will you be 
inviting us on as guests?

00:16:42.020 --> 00:16:45.020
Our budget can't afford Re:vale yet.

00:16:45.770 --> 00:16:48.550
TRIGGER's new show invited us, though.

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:51.150
They've got a big sponsor.

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:54.200
By the way, was there a reason
 you dropped by today?

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:55.770
To torment our juniors.

00:16:55.770 --> 00:16:56.530
What?!

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.220
Yamato-kun, come with me.

00:16:58.220 --> 00:16:59.100
No, thanks.

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:00.120
Nikaido-san?

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:01.380
Fine.

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:06.370
Listen, the reason he declined 
to appear in the movie was...

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:09.380
Okay, fine! I'll go.

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:11.560
Thanks.

00:17:11.560 --> 00:17:15.180
I see that your personality still sucks.

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:19.800
I wonder what that was about.

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:24.230
Don't worry. Yuki is a gentleman.

00:17:25.030 --> 00:17:28.260
Accept the offer. It'll broaden 
your career opportunities.

00:17:28.260 --> 00:17:29.610
It's not necessary.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:30.770
You're a brat.

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:31.780
Sorry.

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:35.370
When I was new, I had 
a senior who helped me out.

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:37.840
I want to return the favor.

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:40.300
You know him, don't you? His name is—

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.760
You think I care about your reasons?

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:44.790
He and I have nothing to do
 with each other anymore!

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:48.730
But you and I do.

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:50.970
He's my senior.

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:53.590
That's what you call an abuse of power.

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:58.300
If I really wanted to abuse my power, 
you guys wouldn't <i>get</i> work anymore.

00:17:58.300 --> 00:18:00.340
Try doing something to them.

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:02.350
I won't show mercy, not even to you.

00:18:02.350 --> 00:18:05.660
Really? You're capable of making 
such passionate remarks?

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:07.630
You're seriously on my last nerve!

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:09.780
How did someone like <i>you</i>
 become successful, anyway?!

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:12.070
Just five years ago, you were 
washing cars at our place.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:15.570
The way you're looking at me like 
I'm trash brings back memories.

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.740
Have you retracted your 
hatred of celebrities?

00:18:17.740 --> 00:18:19.160
Shut up.

00:18:19.160 --> 00:18:21.410
You can't hide it forever.

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:25.620
You can wear glasses, but you still 
look exactly like he did when he was young.

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:28.100
You haven't told the other members?

00:18:28.100 --> 00:18:30.850
Then why did you enter the 
entertainment industry?

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:34.630
At first, I wanted revenge.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:36.150
How dirty.

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:37.530
It's different now.

00:18:37.530 --> 00:18:39.610
I want to make their dream come true.

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:41.590
Gossip about me would 
get in the way of that.

00:18:41.590 --> 00:18:44.310
We can protect you from gossip.

00:18:44.870 --> 00:18:49.100
If you want to make your members' dreams
 come true, you need to climb higher.

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:52.110
You're a prodigious actor.

00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.050
Honestly, I found it frustrating.

00:18:54.610 --> 00:18:56.660
I had to work so hard.

00:18:58.010 --> 00:18:59.960
I heard you haven't been home.

00:18:59.960 --> 00:19:01.530
He misses you.

00:19:02.020 --> 00:19:04.160
Didn't he send flowers at JIMA?

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:07.850
He sent me the kind of flowers
 you'd send a hostess.

00:19:07.850 --> 00:19:10.290
How sarcastic is that old fart?

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:13.540
Well, he can be a bit inconsiderate.

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:15.880
Why did you give up on revenge?

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:20.890
Are you sure it's not because this 
world was more fun than you expected?

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:25.760
Co-starring with me is even more fun.

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:28.930
For you and your members,

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:32.400
you should seriously consider 
the offer before responding.

00:19:32.770 --> 00:19:34.500
Sorry about Yuki.

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:38.130
It's fine. Re:vale is always so kind to us.

00:19:38.570 --> 00:19:42.660
Why are you so considerate of IDOLiSH7?

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:45.420
Because we like those boys.

00:19:45.420 --> 00:19:48.200
We wanted to support them 
after seeing them on TV.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:49.080
Support?

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:51.830
We like TRIGGER and their 
pursuit of perfection as well.

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:57.960
We're inspired to support TRIGGER 
and the hardworking IDOLiSH7.

00:19:57.960 --> 00:20:00.570
While everyone's popularity is skyrocketing,

00:20:00.570 --> 00:20:03.260
there's something I want you to 
look out for, Little Miss Manager.

00:20:03.660 --> 00:20:04.930
Little Miss Manager?

00:20:04.930 --> 00:20:05.550
Yeah.

00:20:05.550 --> 00:20:07.960
As the number of people 
who like them increases,

00:20:07.960 --> 00:20:12.340
the emotions being directed towards 
them will begin to change, little by little.

00:20:12.950 --> 00:20:17.690
You mean we'll start to see 
people who dislike IDOLiSH7.

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:23.070
Not quite. It's always feelings of 
<i>love</i> that make idols suffer.

00:20:24.490 --> 00:20:29.020
The more fans you have, the more 
types of love you'll experience.

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:33.000
People who want the cool Riku, 
people who want the cute Riku,

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:36.470
people who want TV appearances, 
people who want concerts...

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:39.000
Every fan loves Riku,

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:41.530
but there will always be only one of him.

00:20:41.530 --> 00:20:43.930
He can't meet all of their expectations.

00:20:45.390 --> 00:20:49.890
People who work as idols 
like making people happy.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:52.370
They like being loved.

00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:56.230
They take it exceptionally hard 
when they disappoint their fans.

00:20:56.230 --> 00:21:00.230
Some guys obsess over wondering 
what they did wrong.

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:05.600
Some get mad and say they don't 
have to listen to their criticism.

00:21:05.600 --> 00:21:07.240
Then their fans get mad, too.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:10.090
Expectations lead to disappointment.

00:21:10.090 --> 00:21:13.200
Love leads to hate.

00:21:13.200 --> 00:21:16.750
It's no one's fault. 
There's no way to solve it.

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:19.960
But it makes them suffer unbearably.

00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:22.680
Everyone falls apart at this stage.

00:21:22.680 --> 00:21:24.670
TRIGGER seemed to be struggling, too.

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:28.430
But since they had Tenn, 
they held it together.

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:32.890
Tenn is amazing. I admire him, too.

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:36.660
I guess you could say 
he seems experienced.

00:21:36.660 --> 00:21:38.790
Experienced?

00:21:38.790 --> 00:21:42.230
No matter how much he's struggling 
or how badly he wants to cry,

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:46.990
he's always smiling, singing, 
and dancing for someone else.

00:21:46.990 --> 00:21:49.650
It's like he's been honing that

00:21:49.650 --> 00:21:52.850
perfectionist attitude towards 
service since childhood.

00:21:55.620 --> 00:21:58.120
I'm off. I don't need dinner.

00:21:58.120 --> 00:22:01.380
Sure. See you later...

00:22:02.330 --> 00:22:05.980
What's his problem?
He's in a terrible mood.

00:22:05.980 --> 00:22:07.400
Yeah.

00:22:07.400 --> 00:22:10.480
Even though we're all together, too.

00:22:10.480 --> 00:22:13.510
Tamaki, I'm going to 
go watch TV in my room.

00:22:13.510 --> 00:22:16.170
If you get hungry, you can have 
some of the stew in the pot,

00:22:16.170 --> 00:22:18.200
but leave some for the others.

00:22:18.200 --> 00:22:19.750
'Kay.

00:22:19.750 --> 00:22:21.440
Don't play too many games.

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:23.300
'Kay.

00:22:24.050 --> 00:22:26.090
Ah, my combo!

00:22:27.970 --> 00:22:30.130
I was so close, too—

00:22:30.900 --> 00:22:32.070
Is that Yama-san?

00:22:35.230 --> 00:22:37.660
Oh, it's Tenn Tenn.

00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:39.010
<i>Is Riku there?</i>

00:22:40.080 --> 00:22:45.800
We came to understand a brilliant something

00:22:46.390 --> 00:22:52.010
resembling all the light in the galaxy

00:22:52.550 --> 00:23:04.400
Even on days I'm scared, the faint 
warmth I want to deliver won't disappear

00:23:04.400 --> 00:23:10.610
Even if you want to close your 
eyes to reality's reflection

00:23:10.610 --> 00:23:16.180
Come on, let's create an illusion

00:23:16.180 --> 00:23:18.700
The sound of the future

00:23:19.620 --> 00:23:22.840
On the curtain of three thousand worlds

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:26.170
We quietly adorn

00:23:26.170 --> 00:23:31.260
Each and every one of us has meaning

00:23:31.930 --> 00:23:35.220
It's the message of the Fantasia

00:23:35.220 --> 00:23:39.740
You're the one who gave 
me the courage to weave

00:23:39.740 --> 00:23:45.060
So I always want you by my side

00:23:55.720 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:55.720 --> 00:24:00.250
<b>"The Sudden Visitor"</b>
